{"cluster_id": "C-0933", "topic": "The queue's TLA+ posture treats a", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B006-015"], "canonical_claim": "The queue's TLA+ posture treats a batch as a sequence of today's transitions committed atomically; any crash or conflict leaves a durable prefix, and the reachable durable states are a subset of those available from fast sequential `casPut` operations.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-shard-mutation-queue.md#L85-L90"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0934", "topic": "The TLA+ mount model adds `GcFence`", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B007-011"], "canonical_claim": "The TLA+ mount model adds `GcFence`, splits adopt into GET and CAS steps, permits late renewal after expiry, and checks `FENCE-COSTS-EPOCH` plus eventual remount liveness.", "issue_ids": ["P1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-cas-mount-lease-fence-recovery-design.md#tla-gate"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0935", "topic": "Validate-on-hit retention compares every retained view", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B008-055"], "canonical_claim": "Validate-on-hit retention compares every retained view with a fresh `resolveRef` result using `(manifest_id, mutable_files)`; ref-staleness semantics therefore match existing behavior without relying on complete mutation-site invalidation coverage.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-design.md#summary"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0936", "topic": "The accepted residual delta is that", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B008-095"], "canonical_claim": "The accepted residual delta is that an externally deleted or tampered manifest may go undetected on a validated `CachedForLoad` hit until eviction, mismatch, `ForceFresh`, or `StrictValidate`; write-evidence and strict paths retain immediate body liveness validation.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-part-folder-cache-design.md#staleness-equivalence"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0937", "topic": "The combined fix is fail-close promote", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B009-016"], "canonical_claim": "The combined fix is fail-close promote, idempotent republishRef re-drive, and retire-after-removal abandon; reachable refusal cases use ABORTED because LOGICAL_ERROR is reserved for impossible invariants.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-08-cas-promote-over-committed-leak-fix-design.md##fix"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0938", "topic": "The backstop runs after the in-closure", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B009-063"], "canonical_claim": "The backstop runs after the in-closure refresh and owner-liveness check, preventing consequential copy-forward work on an aborting path.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-09-cas-promote-tokenless-copyforward-race.md#L131-L190"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0939", "topic": "The in-closure backstop is mandatory even", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B009-066"], "canonical_claim": "The in-closure backstop is mandatory even if the pre-pass is refreshed opportunistically, because GC may advance again before the closure's fence-round refresh.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-09-cas-promote-tokenless-copyforward-race-design.md##design"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0940", "topic": "Phase A deletes tokened per-leaf promote", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B009-085"], "canonical_claim": "Phase A deletes tokened per-leaf promote revalidation and retained sources but keeps one presence check for every non-tokened leaf, including a fail-closed no-dep arm.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-09-cas-writer-gc-simplification-design.md##deletions"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0941", "topic": "Phase A removes the viewgate drain", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B009-086"], "canonical_claim": "Phase A removes the view_gate drain because monotone retire-view installs and persistent graduated entries make in-closure reads see the required entries without the drain.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-09-cas-writer-gc-simplification-design.md##deletions"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0942", "topic": "Phase A removes the writer fence-round", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B009-087"], "canonical_claim": "Phase A removes the writer fence-round refresh only when its TLA+ newborn-shard gate confirms the redundancy; the GC-side fence_round remains.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-09-cas-writer-gc-simplification-design.md##deletions"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0943", "topic": "Phase A removes redundant writer freshness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B009-093"], "canonical_claim": "Phase A removes redundant writer freshness machinery while retaining the dedup-adoption gate, promote owner check, and one non-tokened presence observation.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-09-cas-writer-gc-simplification-phase-a.md#L1-L20"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0944", "topic": "GC freshness metadata is add-only: GC", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B011-036"], "canonical_claim": "GC freshness metadata is add-only: GC may publish `Condemned` and remove metadata after confirmed deletion, but GC must never transition `Condemned` to `Clean` on a spare.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-11-cas-add-only-meta-fix.md#task-4", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-deposed-leader-clearsparedmeta-fix-design.md#fix"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0945", "topic": "The recovery seal is required because", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B015-010"], "canonical_claim": "The recovery seal is required because `materialization_grace_ms` is an operational store allowance without a documented universal upper bound.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6-design.md#decision-log"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0946", "topic": "The all-tree design closes B123's documented", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B015-089"], "canonical_claim": "The all-tree design closes B123's documented fail-open in which a surgical single-file delete silently did nothing.", "issue_ids": ["B123"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-all-tree-part-files-design.md#removal-semantics"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0947", "topic": "The all-tree TLA+ safety argument refines", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B015-093"], "canonical_claim": "The all-tree TLA+ safety argument refines a same-key repoint into `WDropRef` followed by `WPromote` on a scratch state, rather than modeling the whole repoint as a dedicated action.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-all-tree-part-files-design.md#gc-tla"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0948", "topic": "The Round-B plan required the absence-means-Clean", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B015-114"], "canonical_claim": "The Round-B plan required the absence-means-Clean TLA+ gate to be green before any \u00a75 code and required \u00a75 code to land as one revertible commit.", "issue_ids": ["\u00a75"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-14-cas-opt-levers-s1-s5.md#global-constraints"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0949", "topic": "The MVCC atomic-write short-circuit must land", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B016-017"], "canonical_claim": "The MVCC atomic-write short-circuit must land before routing the former mutable files through the content path; otherwise the tmp-plus-rename sequence would require unsupported rename-of-committed-file behavior.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-all-tree-part-files.md#global-constraints"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0950", "topic": "Refsnaplog objects are written through `putIfAbsentControlled`", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B017-005"], "canonical_claim": "Refsnaplog objects are written through `putIfAbsentControlled` or `backend.putIfAbsent`, not `putDeterministicArtifact`, so their deterministic encoding is a correctness property rather than a byte-adoption gate.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase3-refsnaplog.md#cruxes"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0951", "topic": "Part manifests are `Tolerant` and `Always`", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B017-057"], "canonical_claim": "Part manifests are `Tolerant` and `Always` compressed but are not `Strict`, `PinnedRaw`, or a `putDeterministicArtifact` adoption gate; identity-keyed persistence uses `putIfAbsentControlled` and exchange re-hashes content.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-15-cas-codecs-v3-phase6-manifest-stream.md#cruxes"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0952", "topic": "Deletes are applied to the overlay", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B017-117"], "canonical_claim": "Deletes are applied to the overlay immediately rather than stored in a second replay list; therefore create \u2192 delete \u2192 create leaves the path present in the final overlay.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-txn-one-pipeline-design.md#transaction-model"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0953", "topic": "`CasStore` decomposition is defined by state", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B018-033"], "canonical_claim": "`CasStore` decomposition is defined by state and lock ownership: each extracted component moves its guarded state and mutexes wholesale, receives environment through constructor parameters or callbacks, and must not retain a `Pool &` back-reference.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-cas-source-layout-refactoring.md#L463-L478"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0954", "topic": "Publishing directly under final ref `<part>`", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B019-023"], "canonical_claim": "Publishing directly under final ref `<part>` is rejected because a failure between clone commit and swap would leak an unreclaimed final ref and collide with the generic rename destination precheck; the `moving/<part>` prefix lets startup cleanup reclaim the transient ref.", "issue_ids": ["S36"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-cas-move-to-ca-design.md#L30-L30"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0955", "topic": "The ref-table COW change is scoped", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B019-045"], "canonical_claim": "The ref-table COW change is scoped to `RefTableState::committed` and is intended to be pure performance work with byte-identical behavior.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-cas-reftable-cow-map-design.md#L1-L4"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0956", "topic": "Review finding \u211627 is by design", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B019-084"], "canonical_claim": "Review finding \u211627 is by design: `source absent && destination present \u2192 success` makes single-writer, deterministically-derived renames idempotent under re-drive.", "issue_ids": ["\u211627"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L127-L136", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L47-L48"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0957", "topic": "A CAS test that installs a", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B020-006"], "canonical_claim": "A CAS test that installs a reference-capturing event sink must declare `std::vector<CasEvent> events` before the `Pool`, so reverse destruction order tears down the `Pool` before the sink target; explicitly resetting the `Pool` first is an equivalent but less local remedy.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-asan-battery-rca.md#L65-L74"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0958", "topic": "The safe test fix for `CasPoolShutdown.UnresolvedWedgeSkipsFarewell`", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B020-008"], "canonical_claim": "The safe test fix for `CasPoolShutdown.UnresolvedWedgeSkipsFarewell` is to copy `store->layout()` by value before `store.reset()`; the ASan hit is unrelated to the product scheduler-pointer UAF called codex finding \u21168.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-asan-battery-rca.md#L121-L136"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0959", "topic": "Experiment E1 adds a `TrustedHistory` replay", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B022-080", "B034-108"], "canonical_claim": "Experiment E1 adds a `TrustedHistory` replay mode that skips the O(N) `manifestAlreadyOwned` admission scan in release builds while retaining it as a `chassert` in debug and sanitizer builds; exact keyed preconditions remain enforced in both modes.; A reachable state handled by code must not be guarded by `chassert`: the handler is the fail-closed behavior, and an assertion above it otherwise makes sanitizer/debug builds abort while release builds execute the handler.", "issue_ids": ["E1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#rule-no-chassert-over-handled-branch", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-reftablestate-closed-class-experiments-design.md#phase-c-experiments"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0960", "topic": "Experiment E3 replaces whole-state scratch copies", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B022-082"], "canonical_claim": "Experiment E3 replaces whole-state scratch copies with an undo-journal transaction layer that must preserve two-phase visibility and strong exception safety, while acknowledging allocation failure during rollback as an unrecoverable tradeoff.", "issue_ids": ["E3"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-21-reftablestate-closed-class-experiments.md#task-5-e3-transaction-undo-journal-instead-of-scratch-copy-experiment-keep-or-revert", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-reftablestate-closed-class-experiments-design.md#phase-c-experiments"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0961", "topic": "`TrustedHistory` was initially restricted to replay", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B023-019"], "canonical_claim": "`TrustedHistory` was initially restricted to replay of transactions that had already passed `Full` validation at append time; all writer previews and append-time validation retained `Full` checking.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-21-reftablestate-experiments.md#e1-relaxed-replay-t3"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0962", "topic": "The shipped E3 replay optimization applies", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B023-023"], "canonical_claim": "The shipped E3 replay optimization applies `TrustedHistory` in place with no copy and accepts a poisoned local state on throw because replay returns the state only after full success; `Full` retains the two-phase scratch-copy guarantee.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-21-reftablestate-experiments.md#e3-undo-journal-t5"]}

